# Commits to skip when running `git blame`.
#
# Only bulk, provably mechanical rewrites belong here — a commit in this file is
# one blame will look straight through, so adding a commit that changed behaviour
# would hide that behaviour from the next person trying to find out who changed it
# and why. The bar is: the commit's semantic diff is empty.
#
# Enabled automatically by `npm run prepare` (which sets blame.ignoreRevsFile).
# To enable by hand in an existing clone:
#
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# GitHub reads this file on its own — no setting needed for the web blame view.

